      "a_12_foot_tape_measure_has_marks_every": "A 12-foot tape measure has marks every 1/16 inch. Common usage: read to the nearest 1/8 or 1/16. The black diamonds every 19 3/16 inches mark engineered joist spacing.",
      "a_3_4_grid_with_2_rows_shaded_and_3_co": "A 3×4 grid with 2 rows shaded and 3 columns shaded = 6 cells out of 12 = 1/2.",
      "a_4_point_holistic_rubric_for_evaluati": "A 4-point holistic rubric for evaluating student work on fraction problems. Each level has criteria and an example response. Useful for portfolio assessment and conferencing.",
      "a_5_chapter_story_where_each_chapter_i": "A 5-chapter story where each chapter is a fraction problem in context. Work through the bakery day to apply your skills.",
      "a_b_c_b_a_c_b": "a/b + c/b = (a+c)/b",
      "a_b_c_d_a_b_d_c_a_d_b_c": "a/b ÷ c/d = a/b × d/c = (a×d) / (b×c)",
      "a_b_c_d_a_c_b_d": "a/b × c/d = (a×c) / (b×d)",
      "a_b_vs_c_d_a_d_vs_b_c": "a/b vs c/d → a×d vs b×c.",
      "a_baseball_batting_average_like_333_me": "A baseball batting average like .333 means the batter gets a hit 1/3 of the time. Free-throw percentage of .800 means 4 out of every 5 attempts go in.",
      "a_batting_average_like_333_means_1_3_o": "A batting average like .333 means 1/3 of at-bats result in a hit. A pitcher's ERA, on-base percentage, slugging percentage — all of them are fractions. Baseball was the first sport to popularize this kind of statistical thinking, starting in the 1850s.",
      "a_bee_visits_about_1_500_flowers_to_ma": "A bee visits about 1,500 flowers to make 1/12 teaspoon of honey.",
      "a_blue_whale_s_tongue_weighs_about_1_2": "A blue whale's tongue weighs about 1/2 of a small car (~6,000 lbs).",
      "a_clock_is_a_12_hour_cycle_each_hour_i": "A clock is a 12-hour cycle. Each hour is 1/12 of the cycle. 30 minutes = 1/2 hour. 15 minutes = 1/4 hour.",
      "a_dolphin_sleeps_with_half_its_brain_a": "A dolphin sleeps with half its brain at a time — only 1/2 of the brain rests while the other half stays alert.",
      "a_fraction_has_these_properties_its_nu": "A fraction has these properties: its numerator is 1 less than its denominator, and it equals 0.8. What fraction is it?",
      "a_fraction_is_a_number_with_a_size_eac": "A fraction is a number with a size. Each strip is one whole wide, so how far the color reaches is the value. Turn on the common-denominator grid to see equivalent fractions line up on the same line.",
      "a_fraction_is_hiding_use_the_clues_to_": "A fraction is hiding. Use the clues to guess what it is. Fewer hints = more points.",
      "a_giant_tortoise_can_live_to_150_years": "A giant tortoise can live to 150+ years. A 100-year-old tortoise has lived 2/3 of its potential lifespan.",
      "a_giraffe_s_neck_is_about_1_3_of_its_t": "A giraffe's neck is about 1/3 of its total height.",
      "a_hand_curated_set_of_practice_items_o": "A hand-curated set of practice items organized by skill. Browse by category, or use them as a quick warmup before challenges.",
      "a_kangaroo_can_leap_a_distance_about_3": "A kangaroo can leap a distance about 3/2 of its body length in one hop.",
      "a_medical_thermometer_shows_tenths_of_": "A medical thermometer shows tenths of a degree. 98.6°F = 98 + 6/10 = 98.6. A glass thermometer often shows half-degrees.",
      "a_page_of_fraction_strips_from_1_whole": "A page of fraction strips from 1 whole to 1/12. Cut out and use for any concrete-representational activity.",
      "a_pizza_is_a_perfect_fraction_model_be": "A pizza is a perfect fraction model because it is a circle (so all slices radiate from the center), the slices are easy to count, and the model maps onto the formal mathematical definition: a fraction n/d is n equal parts out of d total equal parts.",
      "a_pizza_is_cut_into_12_slices_1_4_of_t": "A pizza is cut into 12 slices. 1/4 of the pizza has pepperoni. 1/3 has mushrooms. 1/6 has both. The rest has just cheese. What fraction has just cheese?",
      "a_record_of_what_was_practiced_not_a_m": "A record of what was practiced, not a measure of ability.",
      "a_reference_library_of_the_12_most_doc": "A reference library of the 12 most-documented fraction misconceptions, each with research-grounded remediation strategies. ",
      "a_research_grounded_fraction_instructi": "A research-grounded fraction-instruction tool",
      "a_short_daily_ritual_5_problems_per_da": "A short daily ritual: 5 problems per day. Build a streak. Practice schedules beat practice intensity for retention.",
      "a_single_triple_generates_four_related": "A single triple generates four related equations.",
      "a_snail_moves_at_about_1_40_of_a_mile_": "A snail moves at about 1/40 of a mile per hour. It would take 40 hours to crawl 1 mile.",
      "a_standard_inch_ruler_is_divided_into_": "A standard inch ruler is divided into 16ths. Major lines: inch. Half mark: 1/2 inch. Quarter mark: 1/4 inch. Each smallest segment: 1/16 inch.",
      "a_standard_large_pizza_is_sliced_into_": "A standard large pizza is sliced into 8 (sometimes 6 or 10). Each slice is 1/8 (or 1/6, 1/10) of the whole.",
