      "thank_you_for_exploring_cephalopod_bio": "Thank you for exploring cephalopod biology",
      "that_has_implications_for_how_we_study": ". That has implications for how we study minds, treat animals, and even how we look for life elsewhere.",
      "that_s_a_more_specific_order_just_octo": "That's a more specific ORDER, just octopuses + vampire squid.",
      "that_s_a_subclass_only_cephalopods_wit": "That's a SUBCLASS — only cephalopods without external shells.",
      "that_s_a_thermocline": "That's a thermocline.",
      "that_s_an_iridophore_different_cell_ty": "That's an IRIDOPHORE — different cell type. Iridophores use reflectin platelets to make structural color.",
      "the_10_year_old_octopus_featured_in_ma": "The \"10-year-old octopus\" featured in many internet posts is mythological. Wild common octopus rarely exceed 2 years. The DEEPEST known cephalopod, Graneledone boreopacifica, has been documented brooding eggs for 53 MONTHS — most of its post-mating life.",
      "the_2015_nature_paper_presented_the_co": "The 2015 Nature paper presented the complete genome of Octopus bimaculoides (California two-spot octopus) — revealing dramatic gene-family expansions in cephalopod-specific traits.",
      "the_2018_steele_et_al_paper_proposing_": "The 2018 Steele et al. paper proposing cephalopod genomes might be extraterrestrial was widely criticized but generated mainstream media attention. Mainstream evolutionary biology rejects the hypothesis.",
      "the_2021_london_school_of_economics_re": "The 2021 London School of Economics review",
