      "the_53_month_octopus_brood": "The 53-month octopus brood",
      "the_5_mass_extinctions_cephalopods_liv": "☄️ The 5 mass extinctions cephalopods lived through",
      "the_amazing_world_of_octopuses": "The amazing world of octopuses",
      "the_anatomy_of_the_nervous_system_of_o": "The Anatomy of the Nervous System of Octopus vulgaris",
      "the_animal_isn_t_failing_the_test_the_": "The animal isn't failing the test — the test is failing the animal.",
      "the_announcement_triggered_internation": "The announcement triggered international scientific + ethical pushback. ",
      "the_apex_predator_of_giant_colossal_sq": "The apex predator of giant + colossal squid. Sonar penetrates ink + dark water. Sucker scars on sperm whale skin are battle marks. Most cephalopod-vs-whale fights end with the whale.",
      "the_arc_from_tentacle_monster_to_secon": "💡 The arc from \"tentacle monster\" to \"second consciousness\"",
      "the_argonaut_shell_gas_mediated_buoyan": "The argonaut shell: gas-mediated buoyancy control in a pelagic octopus",
      "the_arms_of_an_octopus_are_semi_autono": "The arms of an octopus are SEMI-AUTONOMOUS — they can solve simple problems (like wrapping around food) without direction from the central brain.",
      "the_bacteria_are_everywhere_in_seawate": "The bacteria are everywhere in seawater, but the squid only recruits Vibrio fischeri specifically — via a series of mucus + chemical signals that filter out everything else. Once the bacteria establish in the light organ's crypts, they multiply to ~10⁹ cells.",
      "the_beak_is_parrot_style_two_interlock": "The beak is parrot-style — two interlocking pieces of chitin. It's the ONLY rigid part of an octopus body. This is why octopuses can squeeze through holes that look impossibly small — anywhere their beak fits, they fit. The beak delivers venomous bite (the saliva contains tetrodotoxin in blue-ringed octopuses; less potent neurotoxins in others). Behind the beak: a radula (file-like tongue) used for drilling shells.",
      "the_big_comparison": "📊 The big comparison",
      "the_big_picture": "🌳 The big picture",
      "the_big_picture_2": "📈 The big picture",
      "the_big_picture_3": "🌍 The big picture",
      "the_biggest_factor_in_cephalopod_survi": "The biggest factor in cephalopod survival is hiding successfully. Wild octopuses spend ~80% of their lives in dens.",
      "the_biggest_octopus_on_the_reef_twice_": "The biggest octopus on the reef — twice the size of common. 150 HP, 120 hunger. Slow but tanky. Carries shelters with no speed penalty. Predators see you from farther, but every bite back from you hits harder. Real biology: largest octopus species, can reach 7m arm-to-arm span + 15kg.",
      "the_biggest_open_question_in_the_field": "The biggest open question in the field: what would a TRULY cephalopod-native research methodology look like? One that's built around 8-armed embodied cognition rather than around centralized-brain assumptions?",
      "the_biology_of_intelligent_invertebrat": "The biology of intelligent invertebrates. Octopuses + squid + cuttlefish + nautilus — chromatophore camouflage, distributed neural intelligence, hunting strategy, 500M-year evolution.",
      "the_birch_review_commissioned_by_uk_de": "The Birch Review (commissioned by UK DEFRA) reviewed 300+ pieces of evidence on cephalopod + decapod crustacean sentience.",
      "the_bobtail_squid_vibrio_fischeri_symb": "The bobtail squid + Vibrio fischeri symbiosis is the FOUNDATIONAL MODEL for ALL host-microbiome research, including the Human Microbiome Project that began in 2007.",
      "the_buoyancy_of_the_cuttlefish_sepia_o": "The buoyancy of the cuttlefish, Sepia officinalis",
      "the_cambridge_declaration_on_conscious": "The Cambridge Declaration on Consciousness",
      "the_case_for_octopus_consciousness": "The case for octopus consciousness",
      "the_cephalopod_beak_is_made_of_chitin_": "The Cephalopod beak is made of chitin and protein, similar to insect cuticle. It is the only hard structure in the body of most octopus species.",
      "the_cephalopod_body_plan_went_through_": "The cephalopod body plan went through several radical reorganizations. Each represents a different solution to the same problem: how to be a fast, sensing, predatory mollusk in different ocean conditions.",
      "the_cephalopod_fossil_record_extends_b": "The cephalopod fossil record extends back over 530 million years — among the longest of any animal lineage. They've survived all 5 mass extinctions.",
      "the_cephalopod_ganglion_in_each_arm_th": "The cephalopod GANGLION in each arm (the \"second brain\") contains ~50 million neurons + handles complex sensory + motor integration LOCALLY — without referring to the central brain for routine arm movements.",
      "the_cephalopod_inkfish_industry_employ": "The cephalopod inkfish industry employs ~50,000 people globally — primarily in Spain, Portugal, Japan, Korea, and the Mediterranean. Sustainability + welfare are ongoing concerns.",
      "the_cephalopod_marshmallow_test_schnel": "The \"Cephalopod Marshmallow Test\" (Schnell 2021) demonstrated cuttlefish self-control. The result reset our understanding of what invertebrate cognition can include.",
      "the_cephalopod_radula_has_7_teeth_per_": "The cephalopod radula has 7 teeth per row — and chemoreceptors that taste rasped material in real time.",
      "the_cephalopod_statocyst_is_a_paired_o": "The cephalopod statocyst is a paired organ similar in function to the vertebrate inner ear — providing gravity + acceleration sensing for balance + orientation.",
      "the_cephalopod_story_is_the_longest_co": "The cephalopod story is the longest continuous run of intelligence-grade nervous systems on Earth. Half a billion years of evolution iterating on the same problem: how to be a smart, sensing, predatory mollusk. Modern octopuses are the latest output of that process. Each new species is the current draft, not the final.",
      "the_cephalopod_welfare_working_group_f": "The Cephalopod Welfare Working Group, formed in 2022, is developing international welfare standards. Adoption is voluntary but growing — particularly among aquariums + research institutions.",
      "the_chambered_nautilus_body_plan_essen": "The chambered nautilus. Body plan essentially unchanged for ~400 million years. The current nautilus species (Nautilus pompilius) is morphologically nearly identical to Devonian relatives. A true living fossil.",
      "the_chambered_nautilus_is_the_only_liv": "The chambered nautilus is the only living cephalopod with an external shell. The shell's logarithmic spiral has been featured on jewelry, decor, and curio collections for over a century. The pressure is real:",
      "the_chemistry_of_cephalopod_inks": "The chemistry of cephalopod inks",
      "the_chicxulub_asteroid_impact_and_mass": "The Chicxulub asteroid impact and mass extinction at the Cretaceous-Paleogene boundary",
      "the_clam_is_barely_visible_just_a_slig": "The clam is barely visible — just a slight ridge in the substrate. Slow + reliable food source if you commit to drilling.",
      "the_color_blind_animal_that_matches_co": "The Color-Blind Animal That Matches Color: Investigating Cephalopod Skin",
      "the_colossal_squid_mesonychoteuthis_ha": "The colossal squid (Mesonychoteuthis hamiltoni) holds the title of LARGEST INVERTEBRATE on Earth — with documented specimens up to 14 m mantle length + 750 kg mass.",
