      "admiral_sir_francis_beaufort_created_h": "Admiral Sir Francis Beaufort created his wind scale in 1805 based on the effect of wind on sailing ships. Modern Beaufort uses ground observations: Force 0 (Calm) = smoke rises vertically; Force 6 (Strong Breeze) = large branches sway, umbrellas turn inside out; Force 12 (Hurricane) = devastation. Most birds prefer to migrate in Force 2-4 winds (Light to Moderate Breeze).",
