      "many_songbirds_migrate_at_this_range_w": "Many songbirds migrate at this range, where thinner air reduces drag but oxygen is scarce. Birds compensate with more efficient breathing — their one-way airflow system extracts oxygen on both inhale and exhale, unlike mammalian lungs which only extract on inhale.",
