      "microscopic_hooks_on_barbules_that_zip": "Microscopic hooks on barbules that zip barbs together, creating an airtight surface. When a feather gets ruffled, a bird can \"zip\" it back by preening.",
      "migrants_strongly_prefer_flying_with_t": "Migrants strongly prefer flying with the wind at their backs. A tailwind of just 15 mph effectively doubles a bird's ground speed while requiring the same energy output. Studies show that migration days with favorable tail winds see 10x more bird traffic than headwind days.",
