      "you_finished_the_tool_pick_one_of_thes": "You finished the tool. Pick one of these prompts and answer it in your head before you close the tab. Or write it down. Or bring it to your Crew this week:",
      "you_finished_the_tool_the_most_rewardi": "You finished the tool. The most rewarding learning happens off the screen. Pick one or two from this list and actually do them.",
      "you_inhabited_a_1450_role_for_a_few_mi": "You inhabited a 1450 role for a few minutes. The skills cluster you just practiced — the patience, the craft, the judgment under pressure — is still recruited for. Maine in 2026 has openings in every column above.",
      "you_just_set_8_to_10_characters_a_1450": "You just set 8 to 10 characters. A 1450 master compositor set roughly 1,000 characters per hour, ten hours per day, six days per week, for forty years.",
      "you_make_the_same_kind_of_claim_every_": "You make the same kind of claim every time you open a document and pick a font. Most students never think about this. Pause and think about it now:",
      "you_marry_into_ownership_and_prove_you": "You marry into ownership — and prove yourself fast",
      "you_marry_lena_daughter_of_master_prin": "You marry Lena, daughter of master printer Konrad Müller. Within 2 years his health fails + you take over the shop. The trade grumbles about how you got there. Within 5 years your work speaks for itself + the grumbling fades. You run a successful shop for 30 years + your children inherit.",
      "you_must_produce_a_journeyman_piece_a_": "You must produce a journeyman piece — a printed work that demonstrates your full skill. What do you choose?",
      "you_open_your_own_shop_at_21_a_long_ha": "You open your own shop at 21 — a long, hard climb",
      "you_qualify_as_a_journeyman_what_now_t": "You qualify as a journeyman. What now? (This decision shapes your career.)",
      "you_set_the_type_for_a_200_page_latin_": "You set the type for a 200-page Latin grammar. After the first 50 pages are printed, you discover a typo on page 38 — \"amat\" should be \"amet.\" Reprinting 50 pages costs the master 2 florins in paper + 2 days of labor. The error is small (a tense difference) + might be missed in proofing.",
