      "robot_touches_the_part_with_the_weldin": "Robot touches the part with the welding wire (or a separate probe) to establish reference points before welding. Slower setup but very accurate. Used when part position is uncertain.",
      "robot_uses_sensors_laser_scanners_visi": "Robot uses sensors (laser scanners, vision systems, touch probes) to find joint location + characteristics, then welds adaptively. Operator sets parameters but robot figures out path.",
      "robotic_automated_welding": "Robotic + Automated Welding",
      "robotic_automated_welding_2": "Robotic + Automated Welding",
      "robotic_welding_doesn_t_eliminate_weld": "Robotic welding doesn't eliminate welders — it changes what welders do. Automotive body shops largely run on robots, but every shop still has manual welders for fixtures, prototyping, repair, and complex custom work. The bigger career shift is: ROBOT PROGRAMMERS + TECHNICIANS are a growing role drawing from welding experience + adding programming knowledge.",
      "robots_can_t_go_to_a_job_site_to_fix_a": "Robots can't go to a job site to fix a damaged pipeline or weld a structural beam in place.",
      "root_back_side": "Root + back side: ",
      "root_hot_fill_cap": "🥞 Root + hot + fill + cap",
      "rosa_p": "Rosa P.",
      "rt_is_the_most_dangerous_ndt_method_ra": "RT is the most dangerous NDT method. Radiation exposure is cumulative + cancer-causing. Strict procedures: exclusion zones (typically 100+ ft radius), dosimeter badges, lead shielding, only certified RT technicians operate. NRC + OSHA highly regulated.",
      "rt_or_ut_some_certifications": "RT or UT (some certifications): ",
      "rt_uses_x_rays_or_gamma_rays_to_image_": "RT uses X-rays or gamma rays to image weld interiors. The part is placed between the radiation source + film/digital detector. Denser metal absorbs more radiation → shows as light areas on the film. Defects (less dense) appear as dark areas. The traditional gold standard for pipe weld inspection.",
      "run_timer": "Run Timer",
